 conflict"},{"text":"Child-protection concerns"},{"text":"Workplace exploitation"},{"text":"Social exclusion"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Professional communication should be:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Respectful"},{"text":"Clear"},{"text":"Non-judgmental"},{"text":"Confidential"},{"text":"Accessible"},{"text":"Culturally sensitive"},{"text":"Avoid unnecessary legal jargon when explaining rights and procedures."}]}]},{"heading":"Criminal Legal Aid","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Criminal legal aid is an important practice area."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Arrest"},{"text":"Bail"},{"text":"Remand"},{"text":"Criminal procedure"},{"text":"Legal representation"},{"text":"Evidence"},{"text":"Trial procedure"},{"text":"Appeals"},{"text":"Prisoner rights"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Criminal Legal Aid Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Client / Accused","Immediate Legal Assessment","Understand Charges","Review Case Documents","Bail / Custody Issues","Evidence Review","Defence Strategy","Court Proceedings","Trial / Resolution","Appeal / Further Remedy"]},{"type":"p","text":"The exact procedural pathway depends on the case and applicable law."}]},{"heading":"Civil Legal Aid","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Family disputes"},{"text":"Maintenance"},{"text":"Domestic disputes"},{"text":"Property disputes"},{"text":"Consumer matters"},{"text":"Employment disputes"},{"text":"Housing issues"},{"text":"Government benefits"},{"text":"Compensation claims"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The lawyer should first determine whether the matter can be resolved through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Negotiation"},{"text":"Mediation"},{"text":"Conciliation"},{"text":"Administrative remedy"},{"text":"Litigation"}]}]},{"heading":"Human Rights Litigation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Important themes include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equality"},{"text":"Dignity"},{"text":"Liberty"},{"text":"Freedom from discrimination"},{"text":"Custodial rights"},{"text":"Prisoner rights"},{"text":"Child rights"},{"text":"Women's rights"},{"text":"Disability rights"},{"text":"Environmental justice"},{"text":"Access to public services"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Rights-Based Case Framework"}]},{"heading":"Constitutional Remedies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop strong understanding of constitutional remedies and public-law litigation."},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the purpose and broad application of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Writ jurisdiction"},{"text":"Habeas corpus"},{"text":"Mandamus"},{"text":"Certiorari"},{"text":"Prohibition"},{"text":"Quo warranto"},{"text":"The student should understand when a public-law remedy is appropriate rather than treating writ litigation as a solution for every dispute."}]}]},{"heading":"Public Interest Litigation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Legal Aid Counsel may encounter matters involving broader public interest."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential themes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prison conditions"},{"text":"Environmental harm"},{"text":"Access to education"},{"text":"Public health"},{"text":"Child protection"},{"text":"Disability rights"},{"text":"Government accountability"},{"text":"Access to basic services"}]},{"type":"h","text":"PIL Research Workflow"},{"type":"flow","items":["Public Issue","Identify Affected Group","Identify Legal Right","Research Applicable Law","Collect Reliable Evidence","Identify Responsible Authority","Determine Appropriate Remedy","Legal Strategy"]}]},{"heading":"Women's Rights","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Develop awareness of legal issues involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Domestic violence"},{"text":"Workplace harassment"},{"text":"Maintenance"},{"text":"Matrimonial disputes"},{"text":"Sexual offences"},{"text":"Property/inheritance rights"},{"text":"Child custody"},{"text":"Protection 